# Upgrade Guide

Stay current with the Riso **2.0** template: remapped Copier keys, always-on
mise pins, optional OpenSpec extra (off by default), and quality tooling
(**ty** / **just** / **pnpm**). Visual tokens stay in [DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md).

## Riso 2.0 — 1.x answer remaps

`riso migrate` and `riso update` run **`apply_removed_key_remaps` first**, then
reject leftover removed keys. Do not overwrite a destination key that is
already set. Drop the old key after a successful apply. A second apply is a
no-op (idempotent). Unmapped leftovers fail closed. No dual-path aliases after
remap.

### Preview then apply

Prefer the Riso CLI (not raw Copier) so remaps print a preview. Provide
exactly one target: this project (`.`) or `--answers-file`. `--json` is a
global flag.

```bash
uv run riso migrate . --dry-run
uv run riso migrate --answers-file path/to/copier-answers.yml --dry-run
uv run riso migrate --answers-file path/to/copier-answers.yml --dry-run --json
uv run riso migrate .
uv run riso update . --dry-run
uv run riso update .
```

`--dry-run` applies remaps in memory and does **not** write. Leftovers still
fail closed. `riso update` remaps `.copier-answers.yml` **before** Copier.
`copier update` still works; pre_gen hooks apply the same contract. Do not
pass both a removed key and its dest after remap.

### Remap table

These are the only remappable removed keys (same table as the maintainer 2.0
migration guide).

| Old key | Operator | Canonical dest | Value rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `api_tracks` | derive | `api_module`, `api_languages` | empty/`none`/`disabled`/`[]` → `api_module=disabled`; else enabled + intersection with `{python,node,rust,go}` (`fastapi`→python, `fastify`→node, `actix`→rust) |
| `api_language` | wrap-list | `api_languages` | scalar `python`/`node`/`rust`/`go` → `[that]`; already-list → keep |
| `docs_site` | derive | `docs_module`, `docs_framework` | `none`/`false`/`disabled`/`off` → `docs_module=disabled`; `sphinx`/`sphinx-shibuya` → enabled + `sphinx-shibuya`; `docusaurus` / `fumadocs` → enabled + that framework |
| `mcp_language` | wrap-list | `mcp_languages` | scalar `python`/`typescript`/`rust`/`go` → `[that]`; `node`/`js` → `typescript`; already-list keeps shape, drops empties, still aliases `node`/`js` |
| `saas_starter_module` | rename | `saas_infra_module` | copy `enabled`/`disabled` (also common truthy/falsey tokens) |
| `saas_auth` | split | `saas_auth_module`, `saas_auth_provider` | off tokens → module disabled; `clerk`/`authjs` → enabled + provider; `lucia` fail-closes (no payload) |
| `saas_billing` | split | `saas_billing_module`, `saas_billing_provider` | off tokens → module disabled; `stripe`/`paddle`/`lemonsqueezy` → enabled + provider |
| `include_admin` | rename-bool | `saas_admin_dashboard` | truthy/falsey → bool |

`graphql_api_module` and `websocket_module` are derived Jinja flags, not
removed user keys. They are not remapped.

Leftover removed keys (or unmapped values such as `saas_auth: firebase` or
`docs_site: mkdocs`) fail closed with a pointer to the replacement. Do not
restore `api_tracks`, `api_language`, `docs_site`, `mcp_language`,
`saas_starter_module`, `saas_auth`, `saas_billing`, or `include_admin` in
`.copier-answers.yml`.

## Toolchain: mise (always-on)

Generated projects always ship `mise.toml`. It is **not** a Copier extra and
is **not** gated by `openspec_extra`. Generated Node floor stays **20+** (do
not raise the pin to the maintainer 22 floor).

| Tool | Generated pin |
| --- | --- |
| Python | `3.11` |
| Node | `20` |
| pnpm | `9.15.0` |
| uv | `0.4.30` |

After clone or upgrade:

```bash
mise install
```

## OpenSpec extra (default off)

`openspec_extra` is **disabled** by default. OpenSpec is used on the
maintainer repo; generated projects opt in. When disabled, `openspec/` is not
copied. Enabling the extra does not toggle mise.

{% if openspec_extra | default('disabled') == 'enabled' %}
This project opted in (`openspec_extra=enabled`). See [openspec/USAGE.md](../openspec/USAGE.md).
{% else %}
This project left the extra off (`openspec_extra={{ openspec_extra | default('disabled') }}`).
Re-render with `openspec_extra=enabled` only if you want `openspec/**`.
